WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.680
Even the tightest of ships will spring leaks
now and again, and keeping a vessel the size

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.920
of Star Wars completely watertight is near
impossible, even with J.J.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.190
Abrams back at the helm for Episode 9.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:16.761
The forthcoming entry to the main space saga
isn't due to arrive until December 2019, but

00:00:16.761 --> 00:00:18.940
the rumors are already starting to trickle
through.

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:24.290
If you want to go into Episode 9 completely
spoiler free, this is your cue to click away.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:29.170
But if you can't resist the urge to find out
what could possibly be in store for Rey, Finn,

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:34.039
and Poe, let's take a look at what we might
already know about the next journey to a galaxy

00:00:34.039 --> 00:00:35.670
far, far away.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:37.550
Rey's real parentage

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.730
Speculation surrounding Rey's parentage has
swirled ever since The Force Awakens came

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.190
and went without revealing the details of
her bloodline.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.199
In The Last Jedi, Kylo Ren told her that her
parents were just a pair of "filthy junk traders"

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:54.530
who had sold Rey off for drinking money, but
was he being honest?

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:59.129
Many suspect that he wasn't, and a new casting
call has ignited the debate over Rey's family

00:00:59.129 --> 00:01:00.429
once again.

00:01:00.429 --> 00:01:06.170
According to alleged leaks from ThatHashtagShow,
Abrams and casting director Nina Gold are

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:11.659
searching for a female lead between the ages
of 40 and 50 to fill the role of "Mara".

00:01:11.659 --> 00:01:17.430
The name is an obvious reference to Luke Skywalker's
Expanded Universe wife, Mara Jade, but the

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.490
name may also just be a placeholder.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:25.659
Once Disney took the reins, Mara was erased
out of continuity, but the recent novelization

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:30.109
of The Last Jedi revealed that Luke actually
had a wife back on Tatooine.

00:01:30.109 --> 00:01:35.929
The stars seem to be aligning on this rumor,
but will Mara Jade turn out to be Rey's mother?

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:40.670
According to his friend and colleague Simon
Pegg, Abrams had something just like this

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:43.100
in mind when he made The Force Awakens.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.450
He told Josh Horowitz on the HappySadConfused
podcast:

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:47.979
"I know what J.J.

00:01:47.979 --> 00:01:49.270
kind of intended.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:57.009
There was some talk of, you know, a kind of
relevant lineage for her."

00:01:57.009 --> 00:02:02.280
So, perhaps Episode 9 will give him a chance
to circle back to the still-unanswered issue

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.580
of Rey's origins.

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:05.960
Return of the Hutts

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:11.050
Reddit is filled with supposed leaks about
Star Wars, which means the genuine ones can

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.300
sometimes get lost in the noise.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:18.690
But if a user named 4LOM is to be believed,
though in a post tagged 'probable BS', they

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:23.190
may have an inside track on Episode 9 rumors
via a colleague doing some visual effects

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.320
work on the picture, which has led to some
pretty exciting rumors being shared.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:32.550
If what this person says is true, then the
notorious Hutt Cartel is set to make a return

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.270
to play an important role in the film, as
unlikely allies of the Resistance.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:42.330
According to the source, it'll be Jabba's
son who's step up to take over his dad's shady

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.480
business in the film.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.210
Fans may recognize Rotta as the baby Hutt
who was kidnapped as part of a plot to discredit

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.630
the Jedi Order during the Clone Wars.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:56.610
As described by this Redditor, the Rose, Finn,
and Poe triad will be revisited in Episode

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:02.280
9, as they cross paths with the Hutt Cartel
for a big dinner scene... with a musical number

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.280
in play.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.960
The same leak also suggests we may see Benicio
del Toro's return as the double-crossing DJ

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:10.730
by way of this same grouping.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:16.750
DJ will allegedly be involved with the Hutts,
and Finn and Rose will be understandably furious

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:17.750
with him.

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:23.300
But Poe will apparently see him as a "necessary
evil," and he may even join the squad after

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.290
a raid by the First Order.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.950
Judging from recent interviews that Del Toro
has given regarding the character, it seems

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:34.870
pretty clear that he's ready to step back
into DJ's boots, so perhaps the next film

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:38.070
will give him a chance to redeem himself after
all.

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.980
A time jump

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:44.900
Another Redditor called FOOSLS claims to be
privy to an early storyboard that was being

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:50.230
used back when Colin Trevorrow was still attached
as director, and said there will be a five-year

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.590
time jump between The Last Jedi and Episode
9.

00:03:53.590 --> 00:03:58.620
In that time, Kylo Ren will have fooled most
of the galaxy into thinking he's a benevolent

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:04.070
ruler; meanwhile, the Resistance will have
lost popularity, even within its own ranks,

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.730
as people question why they should be fighting
anymore.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:11.320
It's worth noting that John Boyega has hinted
that there'll be at least some kind of leap

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.730
forward in time for Episode 9 when he mentioned
in a recent interview:

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:19.160
"I can't wait to start shooting the next and
final leg of the franchise.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:23.440
The first step is growing out my hair, so
you can wait for the trailer to see why."

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:29.030
The storyboard also apparently goes into great
detail about a secret ocean-covered planet

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.690
that the First Order uses as a giant war factory.

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:37.540
Underneath its oceans, there's supposedly
a colossal workshop manned by the enslaved

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.600
peoples of countless other planets.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:45.280
And to get there, this rumor suggests Finn,
Rey and Poe will have to enlist the help of

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:49.440
an alien prodigy who knows her way around
the Unknown Regions.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.040
Once they find the place, they'll also reportedly
try to liberate the captives below who work

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:57.410
in the ancient manufacturing station they
power.

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:02.360
As for how the heroes discover the location
of this top secret planet in the first place,

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:05.870
the rumor says there's a surprising mole in
the First Order.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:11.230
Apparently, Domhnall Gleeson's sniveling General
Hux will resort to feeding information to

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:15.389
the Rebellion as part of his efforts to undermine
Kylo Ren's rule.

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:19.980
His brief attempt at putting himself forward
as Supreme Leader in The Last Jedi was literally

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:24.950
choked out of him by Ren, so, Hux clearly
doesn't like the new boss and may not give

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.850
up on his ambitions to take control.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.740
Snoke's second life

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:35.040
When Colin Trevorrow parted ways with Lucasfilm
over so-called creative differences, stories

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:39.550
regarding the real nature of his departure
from Episode 9 started to circulate.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:44.010
One rumor making the rounds was that the director
was fired after he argued with the studio

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:49.180
over the fate of Luke Skywalker and Supreme
Leader Snoke, both of whom he apparently wanted

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:50.720
to use in Episode 9.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:55.180
If true, well, he obviously lost that argument
and his job, too.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:06:00.520
Trevorrow called it "a very acidic situation"
when he later sat down with Uproxx, adding:

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:04.620
"Sometimes creative people can't find a shared
path through the woods."

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:10.360
In what would be a cruel twist of fate if
all this is true, it looks as though Trevorrow's

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:13.250
replacement will get to use those characters
after all.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:18.900
According to Star Wars superfan Mike Zeroh,
a more recent storyboard has been leaked,

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.510
and it apparently features Snoke with a shadowy
figure that looks like Kylo Ren.

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:28.860
There's also a rumor that Lucasfilm may cast
Ed Harris and digitally de-age him so he can

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:34.400
play a younger version of Snoke, perhaps through
the Force Vision flashbacks that Abrams introduced

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.030
in The Force Awakens.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:40.070
This does sound like an interesting idea,
but if Andy Serkis has anything to do with

00:06:40.070 --> 00:06:45.630
it, we'll also get to see the older, disfigured
Snoke again in Episode 9.

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:50.020
The motion capture wizard has hinted that
he'd love to return to the role, admitting

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:54.860
that he'd be "very happy to extend Snoke's
life," and he may be in luck because the leaked

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.380
working title of the film might even hint
at Serkis coming back.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:03.230
According to Fantha Tracks, the working title
for Episode 9 is trIXie.

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.540
What does that have to do with Serkis?

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:10.150
Many are seeing this as a nod to his portrayal
of Gollum in Peter Jackson's Lord of the Rings,

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:12.960
films in which he used the term "tricksy"
regularly.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:18.530
As leaks, rumors, and spoilers go, this one
might seem awfully thin…but Lucasfilm has

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:24.419
been fairly tricksy themselves in the past,
so it would be a mistake to ignore the possibility.

00:07:24.419 --> 00:07:25.699
Back to Naboo

00:07:25.699 --> 00:07:28.630
Last but not least, there are reports that
J.J.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:32.670
Abrams might also be planning on returning
to the planet Naboo.

00:07:32.670 --> 00:07:37.060
There were already rumors that the birthplace
of Luke and Leia's mother Padmé Amidala might

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:42.440
be where we'd see General Leia Organa laid
to rest, but some concept art supposedly seen

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:47.930
by a French source featured the planet's pristine
beaches and coastlines, not a funeral.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.010
Of course, Leia is still alive as of the end
of The Last Jedi.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:56.190
But given the sad fact that Carrie Fisher
passed away in 2016, most are assuming her

00:07:56.190 --> 00:08:00.870
character will be retired with some dignity
pretty early on in Episode 9.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.949
Lucasfilm already confirmed that they will
not be rendering a digital version of Fisher

00:08:04.949 --> 00:08:09.820
for the film, so we shouldn't expect another
Rogue One-style resurrection.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.260
This doesn't mean that the Naboo story is
a false leak, however.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.669
Abrams has previously stated that he wants
to tie all three trilogies together in some

00:08:17.669 --> 00:08:22.490
way with this film, and a return to Naboo
would be a nice link to the prequels.

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:27.160
Also, Lucasfilm location scouts have apparently
been spotted in Spain, which has doubled as

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:28.290
Naboo in the past.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:33.709
Of course, these are all just rumors for now,
so it's hard to know for sure what's to come.

00:08:33.709 --> 00:08:37.870
But if any of these supposed leaks do turn
out to be true, it sounds like the Force will

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.519
certainly be with the film as we follow our
heroes on another fascinating journey ahead.

